# A2/A2.1/A2_03_polite_requests_and_wishes.letz
# Source: PDF slide decks "L2 (Part 1)/(Part 2) a21convlotsmanmeli.pdf" (A2.1, Lektioun 2, second half).
# Slide text was baked into the raster; transcribed from rendered pages, then every
# lemma verified against LOD.
# Grammar focus: the two polite registers the deck contrasts explicitly —
#   hätt- + gär = "I would like (to HAVE)"  -> an OBJECT follows
#   géif- + gär = "I would like (to DO)"    -> an ACTION (infinitive) follows
# plus the five modal verbs, which take a bare infinitive (never `ze`).
# Split from A2.02 so neither lesson exceeds the ~40-60 Element sizing target.

@lesson A2.03 "Polite Requests & Wishes"

# Modal verbs (mussen/kënnen/wëllen/sollen/däerfen) are taught in A1.09 — the
# sequential gate makes it a prerequisite, so they are drilled here through the
# sentences and fills only, not re-taught as Elements.

# --- Bakery & shopping words used in the requests ---
@word de Kuch = the cake
@word d'Taart = the tart
@word d'Quetschentaart = the plum tart
@word d'Bréitchen = the bread roll
@word de Croissant = the croissant
@word d'Noss = the nut
@word d'Nëss = the nuts
@word d'Knäckebrout = the crispbread
@word d'Bauerebrout = the farmer's bread
@word eng Dosen = a dozen

# --- Verbs & expressions ---
@word wënschen = to wish
@word ofhuelen = to lose weight
@word probéieren = to try
@word d'Kreditkaart = the credit card
@word de Comptoir = the counter
@word d'Séisses = the sweets

@sentence
@lu Ech hätt gär eng Taass Kaffi.
@en I would like a cup of coffee.
@distractor-en cake
@distractor-en pay
@distractor-lu Kuch
@distractor-lu bezuelen

@sentence
@lu Ech hätt gär véier Bréidercher.
@en I would like four bread rolls.
@distractor-en croissants
@distractor-en dozen
@distractor-lu Croissanten
@distractor-lu Dosen

@sentence
@lu Mir hätte gär eng Menüskaart, w.e.g.
@en We would like a menu card, please.
@distractor-en bill
@distractor-en wine
@distractor-lu Rechnung
@distractor-lu Wäin

@sentence
@lu Ech géif gär den neien Italiener probéieren.
@en I would like to try the new Italian restaurant.
@distractor-en pay
@distractor-en old
@distractor-lu bezuelen
@distractor-lu ale

@sentence
@lu Ech géif gär mat der Kreditkaart bezuelen.
@en I would like to pay by credit card.
@distractor-en try
@distractor-en cash
@distractor-lu probéieren
@distractor-lu Boergeld

@sentence
@lu Géifs du gär eng Pizza deelen?
@en Would you like to share a pizza?
@distractor-en pay
@distractor-en cake
@distractor-lu bezuelen
@distractor-lu Kuch

@sentence
@lu Géifs du gär eppes drénke goen?
@en Would you like to go for a drink?
@distractor-en eat
@distractor-en pay
@distractor-lu iessen
@distractor-lu bezuelen

@sentence
@lu Entschëllegt, ech hätt gär d'Rechnung, w.e.g.
@en Excuse me, I would like the bill, please.
@distractor-en menu
@distractor-en cake
@distractor-lu Menüskaart
@distractor-lu Kuch

@sentence
@lu Kënnt Dir mir d'Wäikaart ginn?
@en Can you give me the wine list?
@distractor-en bill
@distractor-en take
@distractor-lu Rechnung
@distractor-lu huelen

@sentence
@lu Kann ech mat der Kreditkaart bezuelen?
@en Can I pay by credit card?
@distractor-en try
@distractor-en share
@distractor-lu probéieren
@distractor-lu deelen

@sentence
@lu Ech muss ofhuelen.
@en I have to lose weight.
@distractor-en smoke
@distractor-en pay
@distractor-lu fëmmen
@distractor-lu bezuelen

@sentence
@lu Däerfe mir op der Terrass fëmmen?
@en Are we allowed to smoke on the terrace?
@distractor-en pay
@distractor-en eat
@distractor-lu bezuelen
@distractor-lu iessen

@sentence
@lu Ech däerf net esou vill Séisses iessen.
@en I am not allowed to eat so many sweets.
@distractor-en cake
@distractor-en drink
@distractor-lu Kuch
@distractor-lu drénken

@sentence
@lu Solle mir mam Auto oder mam Bus fueren?
@en Should we go by car or by bus?
@distractor-en train
@distractor-en walk
@distractor-lu Zuch
@distractor-lu trëppelen

@sentence
@lu Kann ech en Dësch fir zwou Persoune reservéieren?
@en Can I reserve a table for two people?
@distractor-en three
@distractor-en pay
@distractor-lu dräi
@distractor-lu bezuelen

@sentence
@lu Wat wëlls du drénken?
@en What do you want to drink?
@distractor-en eat
@distractor-en pay
@distractor-lu iessen
@distractor-lu bezuelen

@sentence
@lu Ech muss Zigarette kafe goen.
@en I have to go and buy cigarettes.
@distractor-en cake
@distractor-en pay
@distractor-lu Kuch
@distractor-lu bezuelen

@sentence
@lu Gitt riicht aus, laanscht de Comptoir.
@en Go straight ahead, past the counter.
@distractor-en left
@distractor-en table
@distractor-lu lénks
@distractor-lu Dësch

@sentence
@lu Ech hätt gär eng Quetschentaart.
@en I would like a plum tart.
@distractor-en cake
@distractor-en nuts
@distractor-lu Kuch
@distractor-lu Nëss

@sentence
@lu Ech géif gär eng Dosen Croissanten kafen.
@en I would like to buy a dozen croissants.
@distractor-en sell
@distractor-en rolls
@distractor-lu verkafen
@distractor-lu Bréidercher

@sentence
@lu Mir géife gär mat der Kaart bezuelen.
@en We would like to pay with the card.
@distractor-en try
@distractor-en cash
@distractor-lu probéieren
@distractor-lu Boergeld


# --- Conditional forms: hätt- + gär takes an object; géif- + gär takes an infinitive ---

@sentence
@lu Du häss gär e Croissant.
@en You would like a croissant.
@distractor-en tart
@distractor-en dozen
@distractor-lu Taart
@distractor-lu Dosen

@sentence
@lu Haut hätt hien gär e Kuch.
@en Today he would like a cake.
@distractor-en tart
@distractor-en bread
@distractor-lu Taart
@distractor-lu Brout

@sentence
@lu Mir hätten gär zwou Taarten.
@en We would like two tarts.
@distractor-en cakes
@distractor-en croissants
@distractor-lu Kuchen
@distractor-lu Croissanten

@sentence
@lu Hätt Dir gär e Bréitchen?
@en Would you like a bread roll?
@distractor-en cake
@distractor-en dozen
@distractor-lu Kuch
@distractor-lu Dosen

@sentence
@lu Si hätten gär eng Dosen Croissanten.
@en They would like a dozen croissants.
@distractor-en tarts
@distractor-en rolls
@distractor-lu Taarten
@distractor-lu Bréidercher

@sentence
@lu Ech géif gär matgoen.
@en I would like to come along.
@distractor-en wait
@distractor-en smoke
@distractor-lu waarden
@distractor-lu fëmmen

@sentence
@lu Du géifs gär eng Quetschentaart kafen.
@en You would like to buy a plum tart.
@distractor-en share
@distractor-en pay
@distractor-lu deelen
@distractor-lu bezuelen

@sentence
@lu Muer géif hien gär de Kuch deelen.
@en Tomorrow he would like to share the cake.
@distractor-en buy
@distractor-en eat
@distractor-lu kafen
@distractor-lu iessen

@sentence
@lu Mir géife gär méi gesond iessen.
@en We would like to eat more healthily.
@distractor-en smoke
@distractor-en pay
@distractor-lu fëmmen
@distractor-lu bezuelen

@sentence
@lu Géift Dir gär e Croissant probéieren?
@en Would you like to try a croissant?
@distractor-en buy
@distractor-en share
@distractor-lu kafen
@distractor-lu deelen

@sentence
@lu Si géife gär fréi goen.
@en They would like to leave early.
@distractor-en wait
@distractor-en smoke
@distractor-lu waarden
@distractor-lu fëmmen

# --- Modal verbs: modal + bare infinitive, never `ze` ---

@sentence
@lu Ech muss muer schaffen.
@en I have to work tomorrow.
@distractor-en rest
@distractor-en smoke
@distractor-lu raschten
@distractor-lu fëmmen

@sentence
@lu Du kanns elo e Kuch kafen.
@en You can buy a cake now.
@distractor-en share
@distractor-en pay
@distractor-lu deelen
@distractor-lu bezuelen

@sentence
@lu Haut wëll hien e Croissant huelen.
@en Today he wants to take a croissant.
@distractor-en buy
@distractor-en share
@distractor-lu kafen
@distractor-lu deelen

@sentence
@lu Mir sollen nom Iessen goen.
@en We should leave after eating.
@distractor-en wait
@distractor-en pay
@distractor-lu waarden
@distractor-lu bezuelen

@sentence
@lu Dir däerft hei fëmmen.
@en You are allowed to smoke here.
@distractor-en eat
@distractor-en pay
@distractor-lu iessen
@distractor-lu bezuelen

@sentence
@lu Si mussen dobausse waarden.
@en They have to wait outside.
@distractor-en leave
@distractor-en smoke
@distractor-lu goen
@distractor-lu fëmmen

@sentence
@lu Kann ech matgoen?
@en Can I come along?
@distractor-en wait
@distractor-en smoke
@distractor-lu waarden
@distractor-lu fëmmen

@sentence
